---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Contact · Foxxe Labs" description="Contact Foxxe Labs.">
  <div class="card" style="max-width: 980px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <h1>Contact</h1>
    <p class="muted">
      Best option: email. If you're writing about a specific tool, include the page URL in your message so I know where you came from.
    </p>

    <div class="pillrow">
      <span class="pill">Email-forwarding friendly</span>
      <span class="pill">No contact form (yet)</span>
      <span class="pill">Fastest response</span>
    </div>

    <h2>Email</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="mailto:contact@foxxelabs.ie">contact@foxxelabs.ie</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Tool-specific addresses (optional)</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      If you use Cloudflare Email Routing, you can create addresses like
      <code>snapshot@foxxelabs.ie</code> or <code>tools@foxxelabs.ie</code> and forward them to the same inbox.
      That gives you a built-in "where did this come from?" indicator in the email's <em>To:</em> line.
    </p>

    <div class="note">
      If you want a real form (name/message) without exposing your email, we can add a Cloudflare Worker later.
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h2 {
    margin: 18px 0 10px 0;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }
  
  .pillrow {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 12px;
  }
  
  .pill {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 6px 10px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: .92rem;
    background: rgba(255,255,255,.03);
  }
  
  .note {
    border-left: 3px solid rgba(125,211,252,.55);
    padding-left: 10px;
    margin-top: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  
  code {
    background: rgba(255,255,255,.04);
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);
  }
</style>
